<title>UK: Russian crude delayed by Ventspils repairs, fog.</title>
<headline>Russian crude delayed by Ventspils repairs, fog.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian deliveries of crude to the Latvian Baltic outlet of Ventspils were stopped on Thursday for pipeline maintenance, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>The maintenance, brought forward from the weekend, was expected to take some 48 hours, the shipper, which runs an office at Ventspils, said.</p>
<p>Loadings of crude at Ventspils in Latvia, Russia's leading outlet for oil sales to northwest Europe, were disrupted for a second day on Thursday because of fog preventing berthings.</p>
<p>Two vessels, Yannis M and Natura, have been at anchor outside the termiinal since Tuesday morning waiting for the fog to lift.</p>
<p>Pipeline deliveries and loadings of gas oil at Ventspils were running as normal, the shipper said.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
